## Prompt 6 — Master Agent: rules-first + LLM failure diagnosis

> **Read first:** `docs/Architecture.md` §11.4 (LLM usage inside Orchestration), §12 (AI Safety / Guardrails), §23.1 (error_type codes), §3 (P8, P15), §31 (ADR-001, ADR-008) · `docs/FRS .md` §3.6 (DIAG, FR-DIAG-001…011, FR-DIAG-014), §4 (NFR-PERF-03) · `docs/PRD .md` (US-07) · `docs/failure_diagnosis.md` §5
>
> Write `backend/orchestrator/master_agent.py` implementing `diagnose_failure(step_id: UUID, error: dict) -> Literal["NORMAL_ERROR", "CAPABILITY_GAP"]` (**FR-DIAG-003**) — exactly two outcomes, no third.
>
> Diagnosis is two-stage (**FR-DIAG-014**, ADR-008):
> 1. **Rules, no LLM** — `MISSING_CAPABILITY` → `CAPABILITY_GAP`; `TIMEOUT`, `CONNECTION_ERROR`, `HTTP_5XX`, `INVALID_JSON` → `NORMAL_ERROR`. Match on the exact `error_type` strings from Architecture §23.1.
> 2. **LLM, only if no rule matched** (e.g. `AGENT_ERROR`) — through the wrapper below.
>
> Write the single LLM wrapper (**FR-DIAG-009**, Architecture P15) that every LLM call in this codebase goes through. It must: request JSON constrained to a fixed Pydantic schema (**FR-DIAG-005**); on parse/validation failure retry the same call up to 2 times with the validation error appended to the prompt (**FR-DIAG-006**); then fail safe to `NORMAL_ERROR` rather than hang (**FR-DIAG-007**). Enforce the 20-second timeout from Architecture §4 / NFR-PERF-03, and the cheaper model tier for diagnosis per **FR-DIAG-008** and Architecture §22.
>
> Budget: **at most** one diagnosis LLM call per failure, and zero when a rule matches (**FR-DIAG-004**, Architecture P11).
>
> **Done when:** given the normalised error shape from FRS **FR-DIAG-002**, the function returns one of the two literals; a `MISSING_CAPABILITY` or `TIMEOUT` error is classified **without the LLM being called** (assert on a mocked wrapper); and a forced schema-validation failure three times over on an unmatched error still returns `NORMAL_ERROR` instead of raising.
>
> **Do NOT:** let any other module call the LLM API directly (**FR-DIAG-009**). Do NOT make this a separate service — ADR-001 fixes it as a method inside the Orchestrator service.

