## Prompt 9 — Checkpoint manager: pause and resume

> **Read first:** `docs/Architecture.md` §11.3 (Checkpoint contents), §14.1 (Checkpoint entity), §20.1 (Reliability), §31 (ADR-002) · `docs/FRS .md` §3.5 (CKP, FR-CKP-001…009), §5 (BR-01, BR-07) · `docs/PRD .md` (US-06)
>
> Write `backend/orchestrator/checkpoint_manager.py` implementing `CheckpointManager.save(step_id: UUID, state: dict) -> None` and `CheckpointManager.load(execution_id: UUID) -> dict` (**FR-CKP-001**).
>
> - **FR-CKP-002** — the checkpoint is written **twice per step**: when a step succeeds, and again the moment a step pauses. Never only at the end of a run.
> - **FR-CKP-003** — contents exactly as Architecture §11.3 specifies: current step, prior successful outputs, pending inputs, workflow state, recovery information — stored as JSONB
> - **FR-CKP-004** — only the failed `ExecutionStep` enters `PAUSED`; upstream steps are untouched
> - **FR-CKP-005** — resume reads its input from the checkpoint; upstream steps are **never** recomputed
> - **FR-CKP-006** — resuming an already-`SUCCEEDED` step is a no-op
> - **FR-CKP-008** — after 3 failed attempts a `PAUSED` step moves to `FAILED`
>
> **Done when:** US-06 passes — a workflow pauses at a failed step and resumes from the checkpoint without re-running any upstream step.
>
> **Do NOT:** expose a public resume endpoint. **FR-CKP-007 / BR-07 / Architecture P9** forbid it — resume is only ever an internal consequence of a successful diagnosis or a verified capability.

